# Server environment variables (example)

Copy values into a local `.env` for development. Never commit real secrets.

## Active / core

```env
PORT=5050
JWT_SECRET=replace-me
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@HOST/neondb?sslmode=require
REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=true
EMAIL_FROM=no-reply@updates.pitchpulse26.com
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxx
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
```

## Authentication email (keep active)

- `EMAIL_FROM` — sender address for verification and password reset
- `RESEND_API_KEY` — transactional email delivery
- `REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION` — gate predictions on verified accounts
- `APP_URL` / `CORS_ORIGIN` — link bases for auth emails

## Optional / archived tournament reminders

Used by the match-reminder job during the live World Cup 2026 tournament.
Scheduled cron is disabled post-tournament; keep these only if you still need manual `workflow_dispatch` dry-runs.

```env
# Optional — match reminder job (manual dispatch only after WC2026)
REMINDER_JOB_SECRET=replace-me-for-manual-reminder-runs
```

Repository GitHub Actions (not local `.env`):

- `ENABLE_MATCH_REMINDERS` — must be `true` for the reminder workflow job to run
- `REMINDER_API_URL` — API base URL for the reminder endpoint
- `REMINDER_JOB_SECRET` — must match the server `REMINDER_JOB_SECRET`
